SUMMARY:Jessie Maple Patton Day in Bloomington\, Indiana
DESCRIPTION:Will (Jessie Maple\, 1981) is the one of the earliest survivi
 ng features directed by a Black American woman. The Black Film Center &am
 p\; Archive has been a proud steward of the film elements\, and much more
 \, since the acquisition of The Jessie Maple Collection (https://indiana.
 us17.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;id=d44e
 e48512&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db) in 2005. Having undergone a 4K restoration\, Wi
 ll is screening for audiences around the world! Now\, Jessie Maple's film
 s are also available to watch from the comfort of your own home on Criter
 ion Channel! Will is included as part of the Black Debutantes (https://in
 diana.us17.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;i
 d=2d70d816f1&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db) lineup\, which is a "celebration of pione
 ering Black women who made an impact with their very first—and in some 
 cases only—feature film." Twice is Nice (Jessie Maple\, 1989) is also a
 vailable.  If you would like to research the Jessie Maple collection\, em
 ail us at bfca@iu.edu (mailto:bfca@iu.edu) to schedule an appointment.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Will</em> (Jessie Maple\, 1981) is th
 e one of the earliest surviving features directed by a Black American wom
 an. The Black Film Center &amp\; Archive has been a proud steward of the 
 film elements\, and much more\, since the acquisition of <a href="https:/
 /indiana.us17.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp
 \;id=d44ee48512&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-sa
 feredirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en&amp\;q=https://indiana.us
 17.list-manage.com/track/click?u%3Df603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72%26id%3Dd44ee
 48512%26e%3D9b80f7f3db&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1769353570196000&amp\;u
 sg=AOvVaw3uI5Eb7-9LI3fQaigo1TyZ">The Jessie Maple Collection</a> in 2005.
  Having undergone a 4K restoration\, <em>Will</em> is screening for audie
 nces around the world! Now\, Jessie Maple's films are also available to w
 atch from the comfort of your own home on Criterion Channel! <em>Will</em
 > is included as part of the <a href="https://indiana.us17.list-manage.co
 m/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;id=2d70d816f1&amp\;e=9b80f
 7f3db" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.g
 oogle.com/url?hl=en&amp\;q=https://indiana.us17.list-manage.com/track/cli
 ck?u%3Df603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72%26id%3D2d70d816f1%26e%3D9b80f7f3db&amp\;
 source=gmail&amp\;ust=1769353570196000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw02d1WcXkcWQiNFwjqaw
 p34">Black Debutantes</a> lineup\, which is a "celebration of pioneering 
 Black women who made an impact with their very first—and in some cases 
 only—feature film." <em>Twice is Nice</em> (Jessie Maple\, 1989) is als
 o available.</p><p>  If you would like to research the Jessie Maple colle
 ction\, email us at <a href="mailto:bfca@iu.edu">bfca@iu.edu</a> to sched
 ule an appointment.</p>
